  "stakes": {
    "do": "Take shelter and a hot supper from Nell Corrigan. Go down into the workings after the bell, which nobody asks you to do.",
    "lose": "Strain, standing too close to whatever is ringing. Adelheid Kraus's whole operation, if Inspector Wexler leaves with the wrong answer.",
    "decide": "Whether to press Gideon Stark for a straight answer about the bell, or take Eulalie's honest 'I don't know either' and leave it."
  },
  "art_gap": "Reads as a grey rockfield with camp props on it. Needs leaning shacks, a collapsed headframe, one lit window and a bell tower. The lit window is the cheapest single piece of art that would change this place."
